pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: the OPB parser negated the degree of a `<=` constraint in the same
% integer width, so `<= i64::MIN` wrapped and the infeasible input constraint was stored
% as the trivially true `1 ~x1 >= -9223372036854775807`. The instance has no solution.
f 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT : ~x1 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
